TreeSet in Java — 4 Real-Life Examples (Indian Context) with Runnable Code + Outputs
TreeSet is the sorted set in Java:

Like HashSet → no duplicates

Like a sorted data structure → elements are always in sorted (natural or custom) order

Backed by a Red-Black tree → all operations are O(log n)

✅ TreeSet is the only one in this series where the output is always sorted — no matter what order you insert elements in.
